[{"id":"fm-core2-2.10-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>Use L'Hôpital's rule to find:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to2}\\left(\\frac{x^2-4}{x-2}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to1}\\left(\\frac{\\ln x}{x-1}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{e^x-1}{x}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{e^{2x}-1}{x}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{e^x-1}{\\ln(1+x)}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\ln(1+3x)}{x}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to2}\\left(\\frac{x^2-4}{x-2}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to2}\\left(\\frac{2x}{1}\\right)=4.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to1}\\left(\\frac{\\ln x}{x-1}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to1}\\left(\\frac{1/x}{1}\\right)=1.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{e^x-1}{x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{e^x}{1}\\right)=1.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{e^{2x}-1}{x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{2e^{2x}}{1}\\right)=2.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{e^x-1}{\\ln(1+x)}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{e^x}{1/(x+1)}\\right)=1.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\ln(1+3x)}{x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{3/(1+3x)}{1}\\right)=3.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.10-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>Use L'Hôpital's rule to find:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\sin x}{x}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{1-\\cos x}{x}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{x}{\\sin x}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{x^2}{\\sin x}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{-x+\\tan x}{x}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\sin3x}{x}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\sin x}{x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\cos x}{1}\\right)=1.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{1-\\cos x}{x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\sin x}{1}\\right)=0.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{x}{\\sin x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{1}{\\cos x}\\right)=1.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{x^2}{\\sin x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{2x}{\\cos x}\\right)=0.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{-x+\\tan x}{x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{-1+\\sec^2x}{1}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(-1+\\frac1{\\cos^2x}\\right)=1.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\sin3x}{x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{3\\cos3x}{1}\\right)=3.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.10-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>Use L'Hôpital's rule to find:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{1-\\cos x}{x^2}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{x-\\sin x}{x^3}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\left(\\frac{\\ln x}{x}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\left(\\frac{x^2}{e^x}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{e^{3x}-1-x}{x^2}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\ln(1+x)-x}{x^2}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\left(\\frac{\\ln x}{\\ln(x+1)}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{1-\\cos x}{x^2}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\sin x}{2x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\cos x}{2}\\right)=\\frac12.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{x-\\sin x}{x^3}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{1-\\cos x}{3x^2}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\sin x}{6x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\cos x}{6}\\right)=\\frac16.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\left(\\frac{\\ln x}{x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\left(\\frac{1/x}{1}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\left(\\frac1x\\right)=0.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\left(\\frac{x^2}{e^x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\left(\\frac{2x}{e^x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\left(\\frac2{e^x}\\right)=0.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{e^{3x}-1-x}{x^2}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{3e^{3x}-1}{2x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{9e^{3x}}2\\right)=\\frac12.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\ln(1+x)-x}{x^2}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{(x+1)^{-1}-1}{2x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{-(x+1)^{-2}}2\\right)=-\\frac12.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">g)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\left(\\frac{\\ln x}{\\ln(x+1)}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\left(\\frac{1/x}{1/(x+1)}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\left(\\frac{x+1}{x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\left(1+\\frac1x\\right)=1.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.10-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>Use L'Hôpital's rule to find:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\sinh x}{x}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\tanh x}{2x}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\sinh x-x}{4x^3}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\sinh x}{x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\cosh x}{1}\\right)=1.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\tanh x}{2x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{sech}^2x}{2}\\right)=\\frac12.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\sinh x-x}{4x^3}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\cosh x-1}{12x^2}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\sinh x}{24x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\cosh x}{24}\\right)=\\frac1{24}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.10-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>Use L'Hôpital's rule to find:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\arcsin x}{x}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\arctan x}{x}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\arcsin x}{x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{1/\\sqrt{1-x^2}}{1}\\right)=1.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\arctan x}{x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{1/(1+x^2)}{1}\\right)=1.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.10-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>A student tried to find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\frac{\\cos x+1}{e^x+2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. They wrote:</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\cos x+1}{e^x+2}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{-\\sin x}{e^x}\\right)=0.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Explain the student's mistake.</p></li><li><p>Find the correct value of the limit.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>They applied L'Hôpital's rule, but it wasn't in indeterminate form, because as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos x+1\\to2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"e^x+2\\to3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\cos x+1}{e^x+2}\\right)=\\frac23.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.10-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>Use L'Hôpital's rule to evaluate <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}(xe^{-2x})\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}(xe^{-2x})=\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\left(\\frac{x}{e^{2x}}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\left(\\frac1{e^{2x}}\\right)=0.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.10-q8","number":8,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Rewrite <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\ln(1+\\frac1x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as a quotient for the use of L'Hôpital's rule.</p></li><li><p>Hence, use L'Hôpital's rule to find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\left(5x\\ln(1+\\frac1x)\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x\\ln\\left(1+\\frac1x\\right)=\\frac{\\ln(1+1/x)}{1/x}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\left(\\frac{5\\ln(1+1/x)}{1/x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\left(\\frac{-5x^{-2}/(1+1/x)}{-x^{-2}}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\left(\\frac5{1+1/x}\\right)=5.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.10-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>Use L'Hôpital's rule to find:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{xe^x}{\\sin x}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{e^x\\sin7x}{\\ln(4x+1)}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\sin x-x\\cos x}{x^3}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{1-\\cos5x+3x\\sin3x}{2x^2}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{xe^x}{\\sin x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{xe^x+e^x}{\\cos x}\\right)=\\frac11=1.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{e^x\\sin7x}{\\ln(4x+1)}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{7e^x\\cos7x+e^x\\sin7x}{4/(4x+1)}\\right)=\\frac74.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\sin x-x\\cos x}{x^3}\\right) =\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\cos x+x\\sin x-\\cos x}{3x^2}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{x\\sin x}{3x^2}\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{x\\cos x+\\sin x}{6x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{-x\\sin x+2\\cos x}{6}\\right)=\\frac13.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{1-\\cos5x+3x\\sin3x}{2x^2}\\right) =\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{5\\sin5x+9x\\cos3x+3\\sin3x}{4x}\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{25\\cos5x-27x\\sin3x+18\\cos3x}{4}\\right)=\\frac{43}{4}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.10-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>Use L'Hôpital's rule to find:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to\\pi}\\left(\\frac{\\sin x}{x-\\pi}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to\\pi}\\left(\\frac{x\\cos x+\\pi}{(x-\\pi)^2}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to\\pi}\\left(\\frac{\\cos(\\frac{x}{2})}{x\\sin2x}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to\\pi}\\left(\\frac{\\sin x}{x-\\pi}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to\\pi}\\left(\\frac{\\cos x}{1}\\right)=-1.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\lim_{x\\to\\pi}\\left(\\frac{x\\cos x+\\pi}{(x-\\pi)^2}\\right) =\\lim_{x\\to\\pi}\\left(\\frac{-x\\sin x+\\cos x}{2(x-\\pi)}\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\lim_{x\\to\\pi}\\left(\\frac{-x\\cos x-2\\sin x}{2}\\right)=\\frac\\pi2.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to\\pi}\\left(\\frac{\\cos(x/2)}{x\\sin2x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to\\pi}\\left(\\frac{-\\frac12\\sin(x/2)}{2x\\cos2x+\\sin2x}\\right)=-\\frac1{4\\pi}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.10-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>Use L'Hôpital's rule to find:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{a\\to\\infty}\\left(\\frac{a}{e^a}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Hence find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int_0^\\infty xe^{-x}\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{a\\to\\infty}\\left(\\frac{a}{e^a}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\left(\\frac1{e^a}\\right)=0.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u=x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dv}{dx}=-e^{-x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{du}{dx}=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=e^{-x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. So</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int xe^{-x}\\,dx =xe^{-x}+\\int e^{-x}\\,dx=xe^{-x}-\\frac1{e^x}(+c),\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int_0^\\infty xe^{-x}\\,dx =\\lim_{b\\to\\infty}\\int_0^b xe^{-x}\\,dx=\\lim_{b\\to\\infty}\\left[xe^{-x}-\\frac1{e^x}\\right]_0^b\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =(0-0)-(0-1)=1.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.10-q12","number":12,"question":"<p>Use L'Hôpital's rule to find:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{a\\to\\infty}\\left(\\frac{\\ln a}{a}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Hence find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int_1^\\infty\\frac{\\ln x}{x^2}\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{a\\to\\infty}\\left(\\frac{\\ln a}{a}\\right)=\\lim_{a\\to\\infty}\\left(\\frac{1/a}{1}\\right)=0.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u=\\ln x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dv}{dx}=x^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{du}{dx}=1/x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=-x^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. So</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int\\frac{\\ln x}{x^2}\\,dx =-x^{-1}\\ln x-\\int(-x^{-1}\\times1/x)\\,dx=-\\frac1x\\ln x+\\int x^{-2}\\,dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =-\\frac1x\\ln x-\\frac1x(+c),\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int_1^\\infty\\frac{\\ln x}{x^2}\\,dx =\\lim_{b\\to\\infty}\\left[-\\frac1x\\ln x-\\frac1x\\right]_1^b=(0-0)-(-0-1)=1.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.10-q13","number":13,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\frac{d}{dx}[\\ln(\\cos x)]=-\\tan x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Hence use L'Hôpital's rule to evaluate <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\ln(\\cos x)}{x^2}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{d}{dx}[\\ln(\\cos x)]=\\frac1{\\cos x}\\times(-\\sin x)=-\\tan x.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\ln(\\cos x)}{x^2}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{-\\tan x}{2x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{-\\sec^2x}{2}\\right)=-\\frac12.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.10-q14","number":14,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\frac{d}{dx}[\\ln(\\cosh x)]=\\tanh x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Hence use L'Hôpital's rule to evaluate <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\ln(\\cosh x)-7x^2}{x^2}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{d}{dx}[\\ln(\\cosh x)]=\\frac1{\\cosh x}\\times\\sinh x=\\tanh x.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\ln(\\cosh x)-7x^2}{x^2}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\tanh x-14x}{2x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{sech}^2x-14}{2}\\right)=\\frac{1-14}{2}=-\\frac{13}{2}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.10-q15","number":15,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Use L'Hôpital's rule to show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to0^+}(x\\ln x)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Explain why we must consider <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to0^+\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and not <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to0^-\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to0^+}(x\\ln x)=\\lim_{x\\to0^+}\\left(\\frac{\\ln x}{1/x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0^+}\\left(\\frac{1/x}{-1/x^2}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0^+}(-x)=0.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\ln x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is only defined for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (in the real numbers). For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\ln x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is not real, so the expression <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\ln x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is not defined. Therefore, we must take the limit as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to0^+\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (from the right) only.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.10-q16","number":16,"question":"<p>The displacement <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s\" data-display=\"false\"></span> of a particle is given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle s(t)=\\frac{e^t-1}{t}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Use L'Hôpital's rule to find the velocity of the particle at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"s(t)=\\frac{e^t-1}{t},\\qquad s'(t)=\\frac{te^t-(e^t-1)}{t^2}=\\frac{te^t-e^t+1}{t^2}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\lim_{t\\to0}\\left(\\frac{te^t-e^t+1}{t^2}\\right) =\\lim_{t\\to0}\\left(\\frac{te^t+e^t-e^t}{2t}\\right)=\\lim_{t\\to0}\\left(\\frac{te^t}{2t}\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\lim_{t\\to0}\\left(\\frac{te^t+e^t}{2}\\right)=\\frac12.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore velocity <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"=\\frac12\\,\\mathrm{ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.10-q17","number":17,"question":"<p>Given that, for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle f(x)=x^{-3}(\\ln(1+x)-x+\\frac12x^2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Use a Maclaurin expansion to show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\ln(1+x)-x+\\frac12x^2\\approx\\frac13x^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Hence deduce that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to0}(x^{-3}[\\ln(1+x)-x+\\frac12x^2])=\\frac13\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Use L'Hôpital's rule to confirm the result in part (b).</p></li><li><p>Explain why L'Hôpital's rule alone is not sufficient to determine the behaviour of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> near <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\ln(1+t)=t-\\frac12t^2+\\frac13t^3-\\frac14t^4+\\cdots.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\ln(1+t)-t+\\frac12t^2\\approx t-\\frac12t^2+\\frac13t^3-t+\\frac12t^2=\\frac13t^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to0}f(x)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(x^{-3}\\left(\\ln(1+x)-x+\\frac12x^2\\right)\\right)\\approx\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(x^{-3}\\frac13x^3\\right)=\\frac13,\\quad\\text{as req.}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{\\ln(1+x)-x+\\frac12x^2}{x^3}\\right) =\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{(1+x)^{-1}-1+x}{3x^2}\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{-(1+x)^{-2}+1}{6x}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\left(\\frac{2(1+x)^{-3}}6\\right)=\\frac13,\\quad\\text{as req.}\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>L'Hôpital's rule determines the value of the limit, whilst the Maclaurin expansion describes the behaviour near the point. In this particular case, the Maclaurin expansion identifies the dominant term to be <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac13x^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, shows how the function approaches the limit, and provides a local approximation with error terms.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.10-q18","number":18,"question":"<p>By considering where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle y=(1+\\frac1x)^x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, use L'Hôpital's rule to find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}(1+\\frac1x)^x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=(1+\\frac1x)^x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. So</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\ln y=\\ln\\left[(1+\\frac1x)^x\\right]=x\\ln\\left(1+\\frac1x\\right).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\ln y=\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\left(x\\ln\\left(1+\\frac1x\\right)\\right).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Rewrite in indeterminate form:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\left(\\frac{\\ln(1+1/x)}{1/x}\\right).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Apply L'Hôpital's rule:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\left(\\frac{\\ln(1+1/x)}{1/x}\\right) =\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\left(\\frac{-1/x^2}{(1+1/x)(-1/x^2)}\\right)=\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\left(\\frac1{1+1/x}\\right)=1.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}(\\ln y)=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, which means that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\ln y\\to1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\\to e\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}(1+\\frac1x)^x=e.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]}]